## Description
There is  MySQL table which has ENUM column. I configured job to sync this table in "Full refresh + CDC" mode to Iceberg.  If I run sync job 1st time ( full refresh) then I see proper string values in Parquet file. If run sync job 2nd time (CDC) Parquet file contains IDs of those string values 

## Steps to reproduce

- create table 

CREATE TABLE sizes (
    id int,
    size ENUM('x-small', 'small', 'medium', 'large', 'x-large')
);

insert into sizes (id, size) values (76, null);
insert into sizes (id, size) values (77, 'x-small');
insert into sizes (id, size) values (78, 'small');
insert into sizes (id, size) values (79, 'medium');
insert into sizes (id, size) values (80, 'large');
insert into sizes (id, size) values (81, 'x-large');

- run sync
- Parquet file has "x-small, small, large"  values in "**size**" column
- Add new records:

insert into sizes (id, size) values (176, null);
insert into sizes (id, size) values (177, 'x-small');
insert into sizes (id, size) values (178, 'small');
insert into sizes (id, size) values (179, 'medium');
insert into sizes (id, size) values (180, 'large');
insert into sizes (id, size) values (181, 'x-large');
commit;

- run sync job again
- Parquet file has "1,2,3.." values in "**size**" column  

## Expected behavior

In CDC mode Parquet should contain real string values in ENUM column  instead of their IDs ( same behavior as in Full refresh mode)

