        "nestedArray": bson.A{
            bson.M{"arrayDateTime": malformedDateTime}, // This remains unprocessed - BUG!
        },
    },
}

// After filtering with current implementation:
// - topLevel: time.Time  (processed)
// - nestedDoc.nestedDateTime: primitive.DateTime  (NOT processed)
// - nestedDoc.nestedArray[0].arrayDateTime: primitive.DateTime  (NOT processed)

// This causes: Time.MarshalJSON: year outside of range [0,9999]
```

The issue is confirmed: the `filterMongoObject` function only processes top-level DateTime values, leaving nested ones unprocessed, which causes JSON marshaling crashes.

